extraction_notes: "WB6 printed 97-99 (cache p098-p100). No amazon class, and no other Amazon, was in production on 2026-09-25. || XP: the Anti-Monster and Amazon ladder on printed 168, lower bounds 0 / 2,601 / 5,001 / 9,001 / 18,001 / 25,001 / 35,001 / 60,001 / 85,001 / 100,001 / 150,001 / 200,001 / 270,001 / 370,001 / 470,001, stored as printed; the book prints a ladder for the race, so it is stored. || POOLS: hit points are standard, same as humans (P.E. + 1D6 per level). The 4D6x10 S.D.C. in non-mega-damage environments is a racial S.D.C. and is stored as a pool bonus, not sdc_base. M.D.C. 3D6x10 + 2D4 per level on Rifts Earth. Both sets are stored, as the Godling''s are; which applies is the environment. mdc_base is stated, so no men_of_arms line. || MAGIC OR PSIONICS: one ability choice group with two abilities, each carrying its own psionics and (for magic) its own magic block, and no class-level psionics or magic block, so each branch arrives whole. Variants were not used because a variant cannot carry magic or psionics. || P.P.E.: the magic option prints 2D4x10 + P.E. + 2D6 per level; the psionic option prints 1D4x10. ppe_base is the psionic figure, 1D4x10, and the Magic Powers ability adds a 1D4x10 pool bonus, which together roll exactly 2D4x10. The + P.E. and the +2D6 per level of the magic option are NOT stored (an ability cannot restate ppe_base) and are in the ability''s description. || I.S.P.: magic option M.E. + 3D6, major psionic, four lesser powers from Healing, Sensitive or Physical. Psionic option M.E. + 1D6x10 + 2D6 per level, master psionic, Psi-Sword and Psi-Shield granted, eight lesser powers (the book says any of the lesser categories: Healing, Sensitive, Physical), two more lesser powers every level from 2, and one Super at 3, 5, 7, 9, 11 and 13 (a second schedule entry at those levels). || MYSTIC POWERS 1, 2 AND 4: read from Rifts Main (Rifts RPG) printed 86, where the Mystic''s Magic Powers are 1 initial spell knowledge (six spells, levels 1-2), 2 learning new spells (4 from 1-3 at L2, 3 from 1-4 at L3, then 2 per level up to own level), 3 P.P.E. (replaced by the Amazon''s own) and 4 magic bonuses (+2 save vs horror factor, +1 save vs magic at 3/6/9/12, +1 spell strength at 4/8/12). The original printing''s six starting spells are stored, not the RUE Mystic''s eight. Spell strength has no bonus key and is a restriction line. || BONUSES: +1 attack, +2 initiative, +1 parry and dodge, +1 save vs magic (spell_magic only, as the Anti-Monster''s plain save vs magic was stored), +4 vs horror factor, +3 vs disease, +10% coma/death, stored unconditionally. Psionic option +1 vs psionics, +2 vs magic illusions, +1 vs horror factor on that ability; magic option +2 vs horror factor and the levelled save vs magic on that ability. || SKILLS: Lore: Monsters & Demons is the catalog Lore: Demons & Monsters 25+15. Language: Atlantean at 98% is a fixed Language: Other naming Atlantean (the catalog has no Atlantean row; the Atlantean Monster Hunter stored Greek as Language: Ancient Greek, and this book prints Atlantean). Language: Spanish 98. Two languages +10% as two Language: Other picks. Wilderness Survival 30+10, Land Navigation 36+10, Track Humans is Tracking (people) 25+15, Track Animals is Track & Trap Animals 20+15, W.P. Archery and Targeting is W.P. Archery. No literacy is printed and none was added. Hand to Hand: Expert changes to Martial Arts or Assassin (evil) for one other skill. || RELATED: the book calls them other skills; six plus one at levels 3, 6, 9 and 12. Communications Radio: Basic only; Domestic, Espionage, Physical (where applicable), Science (Botany, Chemistry, Basic and Advanced Math only), Technical (except Computer Operation and Programming) and Wilderness all +10%; Medical Holistic Medicine only +10%. Pilot any except high-tech power armor, robots, tanks and spaceships: excludes Robots & Power Armor, every Robot Combat row, Military: Tanks & APCs and the three Space: craft rows. Horsemanship is granted because the catalog files riding under its own category and Pilot is any. Electrical, Mechanical, Military, Pilot Related and Rogue none. The Hoplite and Lictor exception cannot be expressed against the Robots & Power Armor exclusion and is prose. Secondary: four, from the same list without the bonuses. || EQUIPMENT: the Manoan service kit is stored. The TW Flame Rifle is the Manoan Fireball Rifle (printed 92 says most Amazon warriors are issued it), with one Manoan TW cell. The TK-Machinegun alternative and the TW Flaming Sword are Rifts RPG items with no catalog row; rather than stub them from this book, both are named in the equipment prose and left out of equipment_starting. The light enchanted chain mail is the Manoan Enchanted Chain Mail; the Amazon entry says 70 M.D.C. where the catalog row holds 75. The tunic or halter, skirt and 1D6 other articles are clothing 1D6+1; the cloak or cape is the hooded cloak; the metal arm bands have no row and are omitted. 50 feet of rope is three 20-foot lengths. 1D6 weeks of dried rations is 1D6 food rations (about a week each). Two or three further weapons of choice (usually matching the W.P.s), and the independent''s kit (two energy weapons, three other weapons, 1D6 spare E-Clips or TW-Clips, light body armor; 60% fight unarmored, 45% of the Manoan service) are prose. || MONEY: usually none; may have 1D6x1000 credits in trade items. Trade items are not coin, so starting_money is not stored."
---

## Lore

The Amazons are descended from a tribe of fierce female warriors whom the
Atlanteans rescued from destruction. Atlantean alchemy and bio-wizardry, with
the help of South American goddesses who took pity on the tribe, made them
superhuman, and they remain the loyal defenders of Manoa. Over the centuries
they have taken on the language and customs of their Atlantean patrons while
keeping their martial spirit.

Amazons are raised to be aggressive, self-reliant and competitive warriors who
use every advantage they have. Many distrust men, who tend to underestimate
them. They are honest, brave and outspoken, see the world in black and white,
and have no patience for cowardice, lies, cruelty or betrayal. On the
battlefield they are bold paladins to rival the best Cyber-Knights.

An Amazon can have children by a human, True Atlantean or ogre father. Most are
daughters who inherit the Amazon''s powers and are schooled in warfare, magic
and psionics; the rare son takes after his father. Marriages are often short:
the wife''s calling and her strict sense of honor are hard to live with.

Since Manoa''s return to Earth most Amazons serve in its defense forces, and
the older war leaders sit on the Council of Elders. Others have left to live
quieter lives, founding small human-Amazon communities across South America, or
roam Rifts Earth and the Megaverse as knights-errant and explorers.

## GM Notes

Evil Amazons often hate all males and set out to punish, enslave or destroy
them, and use their powers to rule or terrorize weaker beings. Amazons in
Manoan service are issued a Fireball (TW Flame) Rifle or TK-Machinegun, a TW
Flaming Sword and light enchanted chain mail. An independent carries two
energy weapons of choice, three other weapons, 1D6 spare clips and light body
armor instead. Favorite weapons are magic items, bows of every kind, Kittani
plasma swords and axes, and vibro-blades.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'amazon');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'amazon';

